# The build stage copies the whole context and runs `npm ci` + `npm run build` in it, so what has
# to be here is the sources, the manifests and `data/dist` (the generated device metadata, which is
# committed). Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or has no business in it.
#
# Careful: a bare `dist` rule would drop `data/dist` and the image would ship no metadata at all.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.github
.gitattributes

# rebuilt by `npm run build`
packages/*/dist
apps/web/dist
apps/electron/out
apps/electron/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# left behind by `npm pack`; `prepack.mjs` writes them again
apps/web/ui
apps/web/data

# the 2.7.1 sources, kept for reference only - never built, never linted, 39 MB
legacy

# the pinned upstream artefacts the converter reads; `data/dist` is what ships
data/occu
data/upstream

coverage
*.log
*.pid
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
